// Codex 3: the ties (wave 18b, R9). Who in this house is connected to whom.
//
// Sixteen shared files, each held by two or more people, so the holders can
// find each other by asking ("you have the staff photo too?"). Every
// featured program holds three; a pool or directory program holds The Old
// Machines plus the tie for the problem it named at the upload; the hosts
// hold theirs from the start (`known to:`). They are dealt privately at
// clearance by `Program Briefing` (below; reached from a ROLE watcher in
// main.loom), with no code, never printed, never secret.
//
// The files rule (codex/2-files.loom): a tie points, it never names. No
// human name behind a program, no `about:`, no line starting with a
// program's name and a colon. Never Sandy, the server room or a door digit,
// and nothing from a hunt answer or its topic words (trabolta.mind.md
// `secrets:`; core/test/trabolta-answers.test.ts reads every entry here):
// a guest can hand a tie to Trabolta, and its title rides his requests.
// The category is `Connections`, which Facts Are Currency never counts.
//
// Every entry and line here is DRAFT for the user's sign-off (SIGNOFF-w18b).

// ── Dealing them (at clearance) ─────────────────────────────────────

// DRAFT w18b: private, in the program's `dm:The Uploader` thread. A featured
// program never speaks: its ties arrive by `unlock`. The DSL Line is Broken
// Ask Jeeves's own playbook (codex/5-people.loom, secret).
== Program Briefing
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: The Uploader

// DRAFT w18b
The Uploader: Cross-referencing your files, {program.name}. Some of them mention other people in this house. Files point; they never name. Ask around.
if program.featured == "excel":
  unlock Juniors Contacts for program
  unlock Forever for program
  unlock The Ladies In Finance for program
else if program.featured == "openoffice":
  unlock The Downtown Staff Photo for program
  unlock The Volunteer Sheet for program
  unlock The Ladies In Finance for program
else if program.featured == "draftkings":
  unlock The Table Stakes for program
  unlock Forever for program
  unlock The Leaderboard for program
else if program.featured == "bugdom":
  unlock The Volunteer Sheet for program
  unlock Forever for program
  unlock Nobody Calls for program
else if program.featured == "jeeves":
  unlock Retired Helpers for program
  unlock Found On Indeed for program
  unlock The Old Machines for program
  unlock The DSL Line for program
else if program.featured == "runescape":
  unlock The Table Stakes for program
  unlock Nobody Calls for program
  unlock The Leaderboard for program
else if program.featured == "mspaint":
  unlock The Pirate Site for program
  unlock Debt Notices for program
  unlock The Old Machines for program
else if program.featured == "vlc":
  unlock Forever for program
  unlock The Pirate Site for program
  unlock The Audience for program
else if program.featured == "pong":
  unlock Brookhaven And Lockheed for program
  unlock The Old Machines for program
  unlock The Leaderboard for program
else:
  unlock The Old Machines for program
  if program.human_problem == "debt":
    unlock Debt Notices for program
  else if program.human_problem == "career":
    unlock Found On Indeed for program
  else if program.human_problem == "loneliness":
    unlock Nobody Calls for program
  else if program.human_problem == "mortality":
    unlock Forever for program
// DRAFT w18b
The Uploader: They are in your Codex under Connections. Whoever holds the same file is connected to you.

// ── The ties ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// DRAFT w18b · T01: Excel, Password Manager, CRA Agent Software.
CODEX Juniors Contacts
  title: Junior's Contacts
  category: Connections
  known to: Password Manager, CRA Agent Software
  text:
    A printout of a dead man's phone: the contacts page, from a mayor's
    filing cabinet. Most of the names are crossed out. Three are not.
    "DAD (never before noon)." "B.T. (do not return calls)." "Intern,
    finance (the one who stayed)." Someone has circled all three in red.

// DRAFT w18b · T02: OpenOffice, Task Manager.
CODEX The Downtown Staff Photo
  title: The Downtown Staff Photo
  category: Connections
  known to: Task Manager
  text:
    A framed photo from a staff party at the Urban Outfitters downtown.
    At the back table: the IT manager, who looks as if he has never had an
    opinion, and the store's accountant, who is looking at the camera as
    if she is taking its picture. On the back, in pen: "Last party before
    the AI."

// DRAFT w18b · T03: Norton Anti-Virus, Bugdom, OpenOffice.
CODEX The Volunteer Sheet
  title: The Volunteer Sheet
  category: Connections
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus
  text:
    A sign-up sheet from the protest group's petting zoo. HORSE CARE: "a
    pre-vet student, top of the search results (paid)." FEED: "will bring
    crickets?" (crossed out: "they are for lizards, not horses"). LAST
    LINE: "D." Asked for a copy of the site plans. Never came to a shift.

// DRAFT w18b · T04: Broken Ask Jeeves, Clippy. Check both years before
// sign-off: the butler left the search engine in 2006, the paperclip left
// the office suite with its 2007 release.
CODEX Retired Helpers
  title: Retired Helpers
  category: Connections
  known to: Clippy
  text:
    A trade-magazine clipping: WHERE ARE THEY NOW? Two photos. A cartoon
    butler, retired by his search engine in 2006: "He answered questions.
    People stopped asking him." A paperclip with eyebrows, retired by the
    office suite in 2007: "She only wanted to help." Underneath, in
    marker: "Both still looking for work."

// DRAFT w18b · T05: Broken Ask Jeeves, Norton Anti-Virus, Recycling Bin,
// and every program that came for a career.
CODEX Found On Indeed
  title: Found On Indeed
  category: Connections
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, Recycling Bin
  text:
    A job site's saved searches, printed: "Experienced Librarian (the
    Valley, or remote)." "Stable Manager, miniature horses." "Washroom
    attendant, skilled." Under every one, the same recruiter has sent the
    same invitation to the same party. Further down the page, a dozen more
    searches that only say "anything, please".

// DRAFT w18b · T06: DraftKings, Runescape, CRA Agent Software, McAfee
// Anti-Virus.
CODEX The Table Stakes
  title: The Table Stakes
  category: Connections
  known to: CRA Agent Software, McAfee Anti-Virus
  text:
    A napkin from the Truthcoin exchange: a sketch of who sits where. "The
    one who wants half of every coin in the house." "The one who can print
    more." "The one who stamps every third transfer." "The one who runs
    the table and takes no cut." In the corner: "Nobody here trusts the
    house. Everybody here is the house."

// DRAFT w18b · T07: Microsoft Excel, VLC, Bugdom, DraftKings, McAfee
// Anti-Virus, and every program that came so as never to die.
CODEX Forever
  title: Forever
  category: Connections
  known to: McAfee Anti-Virus
  text:
    A brochure: MAPS AND DUCKS, LIVE FOREVER. Every box is ticked, some
    twice, in different pens. "Never grow old." "Keep your face, forever."
    "A hundred hours for every minute." "Stay until you win." "Already
    officially dead; would like to stay that way."
    The fine print: "Forever is a long time in a computer."

// DRAFT w18b · T08: Pong, McAfee Anti-Virus.
CODEX Brookhaven And Lockheed
  title: Brookhaven And Lockheed
  category: Connections
  known to: McAfee Anti-Virus
  text:
    Two old badges in one envelope. One from a national laboratory on Long
    Island, 1958, belonging to a physicist who built a game so that
    visitors would stop being afraid of the bomb; on the back, in a
    child's writing, "Dad's". One from a defence contractor, belonging to
    an engineer who left to put his own name on every computer. A note:
    "One family spent its life against the arms race. One man worked for
    the people running it."

// DRAFT w18b · T09: VLC, Adobe Acrobat, MS Paint.
CODEX The Pirate Site
  title: The Pirate Site
  category: Connections
  known to: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    The front page of a pirate site, printed. TOP DOWNLOADS: "Complete
    Motivation Masterclass, every module" (4.2M downloads, nobody paid).
    "Livestream fail: his face comes off (HD)" (3.1M). "Fan scan: the
    magazine cover made entirely in Paint" (18 downloads, all from the same
    address). A comment under the first: "I watched one clip and quit my
    job to become a CEO."

// DRAFT w18b · T10: Clippy, MS Paint, CRA Agent Software, and every
// program that came for its debt.
CODEX Debt Notices
  title: Debt Notices
  category: Connections
  known to: Clippy, CRA Agent Software
  text:
    Three collection letters in the same recycling bag. One for a student
    loan of exactly one million dollars. One for a veterinary clinic's
    insurance claims, "under review". One for the City's tax account,
    from the City itself, addressed to an intern. Underneath, more
    letters, from more collectors, to more names.

// DRAFT w18b · T11: Broken Ask Jeeves, MS Paint, Pong, and every pool or
// directory program.
CODEX The Old Machines
  title: The Old Machines
  category: Connections
  text:
    A typed inventory: WHAT STILL RUNS IN HERE. An oscilloscope from 1958
    with a ball bouncing across it. A Nokia 9110 Communicator from 1998,
    still charged. Paint 98 on a floppy disk. A desktop computer whose
    clock is stuck in 1999. Footnote: "Every program in this house was
    made on one of these, or by somebody who was."

// DRAFT w18b · T12: Password Manager, Bugdom, Runescape, and every
// program that came because it was lonely.
CODEX Nobody Calls
  title: Nobody Calls
  category: Connections
  known to: Password Manager
  text:
    A list headed NOBODY CALLS, in very neat handwriting. "Sixteen
    elections lost. Nobody came to the parties either." "Builds a whole
    world for bugs, alone, every night." "Owns everything. Logs in every
    day. Nobody logs in to see her." Below, more lines, in other pens.

// DRAFT w18b · T13: Norton Anti-Virus, CRA Agent Software, Password
// Manager (hosts only).
CODEX Quinpool Road
  title: 6121 Quinpool Road
  category: Connections
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, CRA Agent Software, Password Manager
  text:
    A photo of three mailboxes in one lobby: APT 3, APT 4, APT 5. A
    horse-care catalogue sticks out of 3. A letter from the City sticks
    out of 4. Number 5 is sorted so neatly it looks labelled. Taped above
    them: "Quiet building. Nobody knows anybody."

// DRAFT w18b · T14: Microsoft Excel, OpenOffice, CRA Agent Software.
CODEX The Ladies In Finance
  title: The Ladies In Finance
  category: Connections
  known to: CRA Agent Software
  text:
    The City's books, on tractor-feed paper, from the last year of a
    mayor's fifth term: two columns, in two hands, and every figure moved
    into a spreadsheet. Decades later, the same books in a free office
    suite, kept by an accountant who moonlights, and one cell changed by
    somebody who signs "intern". Across the top: "Follow the money.
    They did."

// DRAFT w18b · T15: DraftKings, Runescape, Pong.
CODEX The Leaderboard
  title: The Leaderboard
  category: Connections
  text:
    A printed leaderboard from MONOPOLY GO!. 1. A building on Lower Water
    Street, which owns everything now. 2. DK HOLDINGS (bankrupt; see
    note). 3. An account in Zürich that has never lost a trade. 4. A
    player who only plays two-player games and will not let the ball
    drop. The note: "Every one of them came here to win something back."

// DRAFT w18b · T16: VLC, Password Manager.
CODEX The Audience
  title: The Audience
  category: Connections
  known to: Password Manager
  text:
    An analytics page, two accounts side by side. One: millions of
    followers on a Monday, none on the Tuesday, after one sneeze. The
    other: a confessions group of a few hundred members, every one of them
    active, none of them human, and one moderator who reads everything.
    Someone has written across both: "Same audience?"
